    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59884" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρην-αῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρήνη</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of, from a spring</i> or
				<i>fountain</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νύμφαι κρηναῖαι,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρηνιάδες</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.240
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ὕδωρ</span>
			<i>spring</i> water, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.181
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποτόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ph.</u>
				21
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νασμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					225
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάνος</span>, i.e. the
			water of Dirce, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				483
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιβάδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.549
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Antiphil.
			</span></i>); K. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πύλαι</span> the gate <i>of
				Dirce</i> (v. Sch.), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1123
			</span></i>.</div>
